{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>The sons of Simeon, after their families.</b> Then afterward the sons of Gad, the sons of Judah, the sons of Issachar, the sons of Zebulun, the sons of Joseph; when he reached Ephraim he added and said, אלה בני אפרים, and likewise for the sons of Dan, אלה בני דן. And why did Scripture change the order in the tribe of Ephraim and in the tribe of Dan more than the other tribes, to mention in them אלה? It is possible that he comes to hint by the word אלה at the matter of idolatry, for Jeroboam was of the tribe of Ephraim and made two calves (I Kings 12:29) — one he set in Bethel and one he set in Dan — therefore he added אלה for Ephraim and Dan to hint at (Exodus 32:4): אלה אלהיך ישראל. Also, the families of both begin with the letter ש — in the tribe of Ephraim and in the tribe of Dan, which begins לשותלח, לשוחם — and it carries a provocation toward the word שור, and the letter ש will hint at the attribute of judgment, from what is said in the Book of Formation: מ מצפצפת ש שורקת. And it says:" "<b>And in order</b> to show that that sin was forgiven, and all the twelve tribes, which are the tribes of YH, are fit for the Shekhinah to rest upon them in the land — therefore it says, לאלה תחלק הארץ, that is to say: those perished and died in the wilderness, in the manner that is written ובאלה לא היה איש מפקודי משה ואהרן, but these are others — לאלה תחלק הארץ. He applied to them the expression אלה like the expression אלה said of the Levites, who were clean of that sin, as it is written, ואלה פקודי הלוי, and equated them together, to show that all was forgiven."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {0 "The citation from Sefer Yetzirah appears corrupt: the standard text reads מם דוממת שין שורקת; the Hebrew here reads מ״ם דוממת שי״ן שורקת, but the translated text shows מ מצפצפת — apparently a secondary corruption. Translated hyper-literally as found."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:36:19.358570427Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}